Apple is marking India's festive diwali season with <a href="https://www.apple.com/in/shop/buy-airpods/special-edition">a limited edition of the AirPods 5</a>, featuring a rangoli-inspired engraving.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/airpods-5-india.jpeg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070082" /><br/>
The case's design draws on the traditional Indian art form, arranging a decorative pattern around a heart-eyes emoji. The earbuds cost ₹17,900 (approximately &#36;187), matching the Indian price of the regular <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 5</a> with Wireless Charging Case.<br/>
<br/>
The celebrations also include <a href="https://www.apple.com/in/today/event/draw-your-rangoli-on-ipad-with-apple-pencil/?cid=remm-in-taa-diwali-aso-workshop-draw-own-rangoli-ipad">free rangoli workshops</a> created with artist Arushi Kathuria. Participants will use Procreate on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> with an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a>, including a custom brush that recreates the appearance of powder. Sessions run from October 14 through November 9 in India and at selected locations in the United States, Canada, Malaysia, and Singapore.<br/>
<br/>
Sales of the limited edition AirPods began on October 11 and will continue through to November 11, 2026, subject to stock. Customers can order through Apple's online store and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-store/">Apple Store</a> app, or purchase at its six retail locations in India.<br/>
<br/>
Apple limits purchases to two pairs per customer and excludes the edition from other AirPods promotions and Business, Education, and Corporate Employee Purchase Plan pricing. Its purchase terms also caution that repairs or replacements may involve standard-edition &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; with Wireless Charging Case, depending on supply.<br/>
